<%= generated_header("Postfix virtual_mailbox_maps — which address is delivered to which Maildir.") -%>
#
# Paths are RELATIVE to virtual_mailbox_base (<%= MailConfig::MAILDIR_ROOT %>).
#
# The TRAILING SLASH is load bearing. It is the only thing that tells Postfix
# this is a maildir; without it Postfix appends to a FILE called Maildir, which
# corrupts delivery and leaves Dovecot unable to read anything. 143 MB of real
# mail already lives under this layout — it is preserved exactly, not migrated.
<% mailbox_rows.each do |row| -%>
<%= row[:address] %>	<%= row[:maildir] %>
<% end -%>
<% if mailbox_rows.empty? -%>
# (no deliverable mailbox)
<% end -%>
